  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1975-p20.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(BM=CM=x,\\) so \\(BC=2x.\\) By Apollonius’ theorem, \\[ 4^2+8^2=2(3^2+x^2). \\] Hence \\(80=18+2x^2,\\ x^2=31,\\) and \\(BC=2\\sqrt{31}.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Use the relation between a triangle’s three sides and a median",
        "Apollonius’ theorem gives \\(AB^2+AC^2=2(AM^2+BM^2)\\)"
      ],
